            <div xml:id="d468">

                <pb facs="0451" n="443" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg443"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.51/1055: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Chile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-03-09T19:00:00-05:00">March 9, 1939—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>40. The Department has received your despatch no. 526 of February 24 and is in
                    entire accord with your excellent presentation of this Government’s position to
                    the Minister of Finance.</p>
                <p>The Department is now giving earnest and urgent consideration to the Chilean
                    situation and hopes to be able within the next few days to telegraph you an
                    indication of what this Government may be in a position to do.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
